const proposal = String($('Proposal Writer').first().json.text || '');
const requirementAnalysis = String($('Requirement Analyst').first().json.text || '');
const rawClientText = String($('Edit Fields').first().json.chatInput || '').replace(/\r/g, '').trim();

const NOT_PROVIDED = 'Not provided by client.';

/* =========================================================
   HELPERS
========================================================= */
function escapeHtml(value = '') {
  return String(value)
    .replace(/&/g, '&amp;')
    .replace(/</g, '&lt;')
    .replace(/>/g, '&gt;')
    .replace(/"/g, '&quot;')
    .replace(/'/g, '&#039;');
}

function cleanText(value = '') {
  return String(value || '')
    .replace(/\r/g, '')
    .replace(/\u00a0/g, ' ')
    .replace(/[ \t]+\n/g, '\n')
    .replace(/\n{3,}/g, '\n\n')
    .trim();
}

function inlineMarkdown(value = '') {
  return escapeHtml(String(value || ''))
    .replace(/\*\*(.+?)\*\*/g, '<strong>$1</strong>')
    .replace(/\*(.+?)\*/g, '<em>$1</em>')
    .replace(/`(.+?)`/g, '<code>$1</code>');
}

function markdownHtml(value = '') {
  const lines = cleanText(value).split('\n');
  let out = '';
  let listOpen = false;

  const closeList = () => {
    if (listOpen) {
      out += '</ul>';
      listOpen = false;
    }
  };

  for (const raw of lines) {
    const line = raw.trim();
    if (!line) {
      closeList();
      continue;
    }

    const bullet = line.match(/^[-*•]\s+(.+)$/);
    const numbered = line.match(/^\d+[.)]\s+(.+)$/);

    if (bullet || numbered) {
      if (!listOpen) {
        out += '<ul>';
        listOpen = true;
      }
      out += `<li>${inlineMarkdown((bullet || numbered)[1])}</li>`;
      continue;
    }

    closeList();

    if (/^###\s+/.test(line)) {
      out += `<h4>${inlineMarkdown(line.replace(/^###\s+/, ''))}</h4>`;
    } else if (/^##\s+/.test(line)) {
      out += `<h3>${inlineMarkdown(line.replace(/^##\s+/, ''))}</h3>`;
    } else if (/^#\s+/.test(line)) {
      out += `<h2>${inlineMarkdown(line.replace(/^#\s+/, ''))}</h2>`;
    } else {
      out += `<p>${inlineMarkdown(line)}</p>`;
    }
  }

  closeList();
  return out || `<p>${escapeHtml(NOT_PROVIDED)}</p>`;
}

function getSection(name, fallback = NOT_PROVIDED) {
  const lines = cleanText(proposal).split('\n');
  const target = String(name).trim().toLowerCase();
  const headings = [
    'Proposal Title',
    'Short Professional Subtitle',
    'Prepared By',
    'Date',
    'Executive Summary',
    'Client Understanding',
    'Current Challenges',
    'Business Goals',
    'Proposed Solution',
    'Key Modules',
    'Important Features',
    'Business Workflow',
    'Implementation Plan',
    'Deliverables',
    'Expected Benefits',
    'Reports and Dashboard Requirements',
    'Investment and Pricing',
    'Assumptions',
    'Terms and Conditions',
    'Next Steps',
    'Contact Information'
  ].map(x => x.toLowerCase());

  let start = -1;

  for (let i = 0; i < lines.length; i++) {
    const normalized = lines[i]
      .replace(/^\s*(?:#{1,6}\s*)?/, '')
      .replace(/\*\*/g, '')
      .replace(/:$/, '')
      .trim()
      .toLowerCase();

    if (normalized === target) {
      start = i + 1;
      break;
    }
  }

  if (start === -1) return fallback;

  const collected = [];

  for (let i = start; i < lines.length; i++) {
    const normalized = lines[i]
      .replace(/^\s*(?:#{1,6}\s*)?/, '')
      .replace(/\*\*/g, '')
      .replace(/:$/, '')
      .trim()
      .toLowerCase();

    if (headings.includes(normalized)) break;
    collected.push(lines[i]);
  }

  const result = cleanText(collected.join('\n'));
  return result || fallback;
}

function getLabeled(source, labels, fallback = NOT_PROVIDED) {
  const text = cleanText(source);
  for (const label of labels) {
    const re = new RegExp(
      '^\\s*' + label.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\]\\]/g, '\\$&') + '\\s*:\\s*(.+)$',
      'im'
    );
    const match = text.match(re);
    if (match && match[1].trim()) return match[1].trim();
  }
  return fallback;
}

function bullets(value = '') {
  const text = cleanText(value);
  if (!text || text === NOT_PROVIDED) return [NOT_PROVIDED];

  const lines = text.split('\n').map(x => x.trim()).filter(Boolean);
  const items = [];

  for (const line of lines) {
    const m = line.match(/^(?:[-*•]|\d+[.)])\s+(.+)$/);
    if (m) items.push(m[1].trim());
  }

  if (items.length) return items;

  // If AI returned paragraphs instead of bullets, preserve the wording
  // while creating compact visual items.
  return text
    .split(/\n\n+/)
    .map(x => x.replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim())
    .filter(Boolean);
}

function compact(value, max = 430) {
  const text = cleanText(value).replace(/\s+/g, ' ');
  if (text.length <= max) return text;
  return text.slice(0, max - 1).trimEnd() + '…';
}

function titleFromItem(item) {
  const text = cleanText(item);
  const split = text.split(/\s*[:—–-]\s*/);
  if (split.length > 1 && split[0].length <= 55) {
    return split[0];
  }
  return text.length > 48 ? text.slice(0, 48).trimEnd() + '…' : text;
}

function bodyFromItem(item) {
  const text = cleanText(item);
  const split = text.split(/\s*[:—–-]\s*/);
  if (split.length > 1 && split[0].length <= 55) {
    return split.slice(1).join(' — ');
  }
  return '';
}

function firstUseful(items, fallback = NOT_PROVIDED) {
  return items.find(x => x && x !== NOT_PROVIDED) || fallback;
}

/* =========================================================
   RAW CLIENT DOCUMENT MODE
   Preserve client-provided long quotation wording.
========================================================= */
function rawInline(text) {
  return inlineMarkdown(text);
}

function rawDocumentToHtml(text) {
  const lines = cleanText(text).split('\n');
  let out = '';
  let list = false;

  const close = () => {
    if (list) {
      out += '</ul>';
      list = false;
    }
  };

  for (const raw of lines) {
    const line = raw.trim();
    if (!line) {
      close();
      out += '<div class="raw-gap"></div>';
      continue;
    }

    const bullet = line.match(/^[-*•]\s+(.+)$/);
    const numbered = line.match(/^\d+[.)]\s+(.+)$/);

    if (bullet || numbered) {
      if (!list) {
        out += '<ul>';
        list = true;
      }
      out += `<li>${rawInline((bullet || numbered)[1])}</li>`;
      continue;
    }

    close();

    if (/^#\s+/.test(line)) {
      out += `<h1>${rawInline(line.replace(/^#\s+/, ''))}</h1>`;
    } else if (/^##\s+/.test(line)) {
      out += `<h2>${rawInline(line.replace(/^##\s+/, ''))}</h2>`;
    } else if (/^###\s+/.test(line)) {
      out += `<h3>${rawInline(line.replace(/^###\s+/, ''))}</h3>`;
    } else if (/^---+$/.test(line)) {
      out += '<hr>';
    } else {
      out += `<p>${rawInline(line)}</p>`;
    }
  }

  close();
  return out;
}

